Notebook[
 {Cell[CellGroupData[
    {Cell["SM Five-Point Construction and Independent Validation", "Title"],
     Cell["Construct the five-point SM amplitudes from elementary diagrams \
and complete lower-point factorization amplitudes. Each construction checks \
physical poles, spurious-pole cancellation, high-energy behavior, reference \
independence and independent Feynman diagrams. Each process family has its \
own SPINAS export with CalcHEP and MadGraph comparisons.", "Text"],
     Cell["All construction momenta are ingoing. The export states a physical \
two-to-three process and crosses the outgoing particles consistently. Photon \
and gluon helicities remain explicit; the numerical comparisons perform the \
required spin and color sums.", "Text"],
     Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Setup", "Section"], Cell["hepcatDirectory = \
ExpandFileName[\"~/code/hepcat\"];\nGet[FileNameJoin[{hepcatDirectory, \
\"source\", \"HEPCAT.wl\"}]]", "Input", CellTags -> "sm5-setup-load"],
        Cell["sm = ReadModel[FileNameJoin[{hepcatDirectory, \"models\"}], \
1];\nsmFactorization = ReadModel[FileNameJoin[{hepcatDirectory, \"models\"}], \
2];\nsmFeynman = ReadModel[FileNameJoin[{hepcatDirectory, \"tests\", \
\"reference-models\", \"calchep\"}], 1];", "Input", CellTags ->
          "sm5-setup-models"], Cell["Model 1 supplies elementary SM \
interactions for the diagrams. Model 2 supplies complete four-point \
amplitudes for the five-point factorization channels. The Feynman calculation \
uses the separate SM Feynman-rule model. Change the paths below to match your \
installation. Independent numerical comparisons match the parameters and turn \
off widths in their private benchmark copies.", "Text"],
        Cell["spinasDirectory = \
FileNameJoin[{ParentDirectory[hepcatDirectory], \
\"spinas\"}];\nspinasOutputDirectory = FileNameJoin[{hepcatDirectory, \
\"tests\", \"results\", \"spinas-output\", \
\"SM-5-point\"}];\ncalcHEPDirectory = \
FileNameJoin[{ParentDirectory[hepcatDirectory], \"CalcHEP\", \
\"calchep_3.9.2\"}];\ncalcHEPModel = {FileNameJoin[{hepcatDirectory, \
\"tests\", \"reference-models\", \"calchep\"}], 1};\nmadGraphDirectory = \
FileNameJoin[{ParentDirectory[hepcatDirectory], \
\"MadGraph\"}];\nmadGraphModel = FileNameJoin[{hepcatDirectory, \"tests\", \
\"reference-models\", \"madgraph\", \"sm\"}];\nmadGraphParameterRules = \
{\"lamWS\" -> 0};\nvalidationPoints = 1000;\nvalidationOptions = {\n  \
\"SPINASDirectory\" -> spinasDirectory,\n  \"Build\" -> True, \"RunExamples\" \
-> True, \"Overwrite\" -> True,\n  \"CalcHEPDirectory\" -> calcHEPDirectory, \
\"CalcHEPModel\" -> calcHEPModel,\n  \"CalcHEPPoints\" -> validationPoints, \
\"RunCalcHEPValidation\" -> True,\n  \"MadGraphDirectory\" -> \
madGraphDirectory, \"MadGraphModel\" -> madGraphModel,\n  \
\"MadGraphParameterRules\" -> madGraphParameterRules,\n  \"MadGraphPoints\" \
-> validationPoints, \"RunMadGraphValidation\" -> True,\n  \"ReturnDetails\" \
-> True};", "Input", CellTags -> "sm5-setup-validation"],
        Cell["Both reference programs retain the full SM. The lamWS setting \
selects diagonal quark flavor mixing to match the constructive model. The \
massive-quark reference models include their Higgs couplings. No \
electron/photon-only restriction is applied.", "Text"]}, Open]],
     Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Sector overview", "Section"],
        Cell["The full inventory contains 1422 construction cases in 869 \
export families. This notebook develops the sectors in stages. The explicit \
calculations below cover 16 families; the remaining families are listed in \
tests/SM-5-point/inventory.json. Validation results appear after each \
calculation or comparison runs.", "Text"], Cell["The cells retain output only \
from actual captured runs. Missing output means the cell has not been run \
here. Evaluate Setup, then an amplitude cell, then its family export to \
obtain fresh construction and numerical comparison tables.", "Text"],
        Cell["Higgs amplitudes: 1 export family, 1 construction case.",
         "Text"], Cell["Higgs and massive electroweak vectors: 8 export \
families, 8 construction cases.", "Text"], Cell["Electroweak amplitudes with \
photons: 7 export families, 18 construction cases.", "Text"],
        Cell["Gluons: 1 export family, 6 construction cases.", "Text"],
        Cell["Two fermions with Higgs bosons: 108 export families, 156 \
construction cases.", "Text"], Cell["Two fermions and electroweak bosons: 111 \
export families, 213 construction cases.", "Text"],
        Cell["Two fermions and QCD bosons: 90 export families, 294 \
construction cases.", "Text"], Cell["Four fermions with a Higgs boson: 108 \
export families, 108 construction cases.", "Text"], Cell["Four fermions with \
a massive electroweak vector: 252 export families, 252 construction cases.",
         "Text"], Cell["Four fermions with a photon: 102 export families, 204 \
construction cases.", "Text"],
        Cell["Four fermions with a gluon: 81 export families, 162 \
construction cases.", "Text"]}, Open]],
     Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Higgs amplitudes", "Section",
         CellTags -> "sm5-sector-PureHiggs"],
        Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["h, h, h, h, h", "Subsection",
            CellTags -> "sm5-family-sm5f_7f553e102e15"], Cell["Physical \
export: h, h -> h, h, h. The construction lists below use all momenta \
